## FAQs

### What do I need to rent for an outdoor wedding?

A full outdoor wedding rental list usually spans tents, seating, catering equipment, decor and AV. Malaga Event Gear supplies only the last category, through the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/): PA sound, ambient lighting, wireless microphones and a live technician. Tents, furniture, restrooms and decor need a separate vendor.

### Do I need a permit for outdoor wedding sound in Malaga?

We do not handle permits or negotiate curfews with your venue. Confirm any noise curfew or amplified sound restriction with your venue before booking, common at fincas and villas around Malaga, and tell us the curfew so our live technician can size and time the sound system around it.

### How much sound power does an outdoor wedding need compared to indoors?

Open air disperses sound further than an indoor room does, since there are no walls to reflect off, so an outdoor PA is set up to project across the space rather than fill a room. A wedding adds ceremony and reception zones on top of that, usually with different sound needs, which is why a live technician stays for both rather than leaving a single fixed setup.

### Do I need a generator for an outdoor wedding?

We do not stock generators. Confirm your venue's power access with us when you book, especially for a remote finca or a beach location, and we will size the setup to what is actually available.

### How does wind affect outdoor wedding sound and lighting?

Wind on a coastal terrace or an open lawn affects where a speaker stand or lighting rig can safely stand, and how far sound carries. Our technician reads wind exposure and ground surface on site and places equipment accordingly.

### What guest count fits an outdoor wedding AV setup?

Guest count decides the package, not tent square footage. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) suits up to 50 guests, self run after our crew delivers and tests it. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) suits up to 80 guests, with a live technician on site throughout, which matters more outdoors where wind, curfews and ceremony to reception transitions all need adjusting on the day.

### What's different about planning AV for an outdoor wedding versus an indoor one?

Four things: sound projects across open space instead of filling a room with walls to reflect off, venue power needs confirming since we do not stock generators, many fincas and villas set a curfew on amplified sound that an indoor venue may not, and equipment placement has to account for wind and ground surface rather than a fixed indoor layout.
